** femahoy M2 assembly fixture: one part, 3 instances, one model.
** Part BAR is a unit cube of C3D8I, E = 1000, nu = 0.3. Instances I1 and I2 sit end to end
** along x (I2 is moved by 1) and *MPC TIE joins their touching faces. Instance I3 is moved
** by 5 in y and has no link to the others. Each instance has the support of a tension bar.
** Pull 100 on the end face of I2 and 50 on the end face of I3. The exact solution is a
** uniform tension in each bar: sxx = 100 in I1 and I2, sxx = 50 in I3, with
** u = (0.1 x, -0.03 y, -0.03 z) over I1 and I2, and u = (0.05 x, -0.015 (y - 5), -0.015 z) in I3.
